\name{BaseRRocrPerformanceLayerProcessor}
\alias{BaseRRocrPerformanceLayerProcessor}
\title{Base R ROCR Performance Layer Processor}
\description{
Reads \code{plot()} of a ROCR \code{performance} object -- most often
\code{plot(performance(pred, "prec", "rec"))}, a precision-recall curve -- from
the object itself.
\subsection{Why the object and not the drawing}{

ROCR's \code{plot} method draws with calls made from inside its own namespace:
\code{.performance.plot.canvas()} calls \code{plot()} with \code{type = "n"}, \code{axis()}
and \code{box()}, and \code{.performance.plot.no.avg()} draws each curve with
\code{plot.xy()} (ROCR 1.0.11). Those resolve through ROCR's imports of
graphics, never through the search path, so maidr's wrappers see none of
them; what is recorded is the one \code{plot(perf)} call the reader wrote. Its
\code{x.values} and \code{y.values} are the points the method draws, after it drops
the pairs that are not finite (\code{ROCR:::.plot.performance}), as this does
too; its \code{x.name} and \code{y.name} are the axis titles it draws unless
\code{xlab} and \code{ylab} are given.
}

\subsection{The reading}{

ROCR names the axes of \code{performance(pred, "prec", "rec")} "Recall" and
"Precision", so the curve is a precision-recall curve by its own titles
(\code{\link[=titled_pr_curve]{titled_pr_curve()}}), as \code{plot(recall, precision, type = "l")} is, and is
emitted as a \code{pr_curve} layer whose points carry the cutoff each was
scored at, from \code{alpha.values}. ROCR scores its first point at an infinite
cutoff, which has no JSON number and is left out. Every other measure ROCR
plots against another -- a ROC curve's rates, accuracy against cutoff --
is a line, which is what it draws.

One series per run: a \code{performance} object of several runs (from
cross-validation) draws one curve each, with \code{plot.xy()}, and gridGraphics
names each \code{graphics-plot-N-lines-M}, the polylines the line processor
finds -- so highlighting needs nothing new.

Only the plain drawing is read; see \code{\link[=rocr_performance_layer_type]{rocr_performance_layer_type()}} for
what is declined.
}
}
